==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{confix|en|diplo|oid}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪd}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|genetics}} Of a cell, having a pair of each type of [[chromosome]], one of the pair being derived from the [[ovum]] and the other from the [[spermatozoon]]. Most [[somatic cell]]s of higher organisms are diploid.
# {{lb|en|genetics}} Of an organism, having diploid cells.
# {{lb|en|crystallography}} Of a certain [[symmetry]] [[class]] with 24 [[congruent]] [[irregular]] [[quadrilateral]] [[face]]s.

